      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Prediction is pass: direct in-vivo brain detection after systemic administration is consistently reported for multiple close analogues (procyanidin B2, taxifolin, EGCG, naringenin, hesperetin), while the only negative record is from a much less similar compound and does not override the positive analogue evidence.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific brain exposure data; inference relies on structural analogues.",
    "One negative record (medicarpin) at low similarity and one EGCG record labeling 0.5 nmol/g as poor penetration create minor inconsistency, but direct brain detection still supports access."
  ],
